# core-vendor.manifest — the pin. Names ONE commit of
# agenticapps-eu/agenticapps-workflow-core and a sha256 per file.
# Read by bin/resolve-core-artifact.sh and by migrations/run-tests.sh
# (test_core_artifacts_resolve_from_pin). Do NOT hand-edit a sha: re-pin by
# recomputing every entry at the new commit.
#
# core_commit is a COMMIT, not a branch. A core checkout is a live workspace
# and may sit mid-change on a feature branch, and origin/main can advance
# BETWEEN two commands. Resolve it ONCE and take every file from that one
# revision — a per-file rev-parse is how the gate and the harness ended up
# from different commits on 2026-07-25.
#
# ONE commit covers EVERY file listed, and every file this repo takes from
# core is listed. Consistency among the entries present is not sufficient: a
# manifest naming four of seven files is internally consistent while recording
# nothing about the three it omits.
#
# Advancing core_commit therefore means RE-VERIFYING the files already listed
# at the new revision, not just appending the new ones.
#
# ── two categories, deliberately different ───────────────────────────────────
#
# RESOLVED — install.sh and migration 0032 publish these into the shared
#   ~/.agenticapps/bin/. They are NOT vendored in this repo. Vendoring them is
#   what ADR-0047 removed: the runtime never read the copies, so they existed
#   only to feed the installer, and they drifted. On 2026-07-31 all three were
#   stale at once (gate 1.3.1 vs 2.0.0, producer 1.0.0 vs 1.2.0, wrapper 1.1.0
#   vs 1.2.0) and the suite was red for exactly that.
#
# VENDORED — still on disk, because each has a reason it cannot be resolved:
#   resolve-core-artifact.sh is the bootstrap and cannot resolve itself;
#   install-shared-artifact.sh is invoked by hand during a publication; the two
#   conformance harnesses are executed from the repo by CI. They are pinned
#   anyway, and the test compares the bytes on disk to the bytes named here.
#
# ── the pin ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ef030d0 is core's main at the merge of PR #49 — the merge commit itself. It
# carries gate 2.0.0, producer 1.2.0, wrapper 1.2.0 and shared-install 1.0.1,
# all four unchanged from the previous pin, plus core spec 1.4.0 / §20: a
# conformance harness that scored nothing is no longer green. Both harnesses
# now report `UNSCOREABLE <label> — <reason>` and fail on a named target that
# is absent, empty or unreadable, instead of exiting 0 having certified
# nothing.
#
# The previous pin, 6cd3b9c, is why that matters here. It resolved the two
# harnesses as they stood BEFORE that fix — the exact defect ADR-0047 recorded
# as a known limit and deferred to core, worked around in this repo with a
# `test -s` after each resolve in `openspec-gate.yml`. Until this re-pin, the
# fix was merged in core and had reached no host.
#
# All seven entries below were re-verified at ef030d0. Five are byte-identical
# to 6cd3b9c; the two vendored harnesses changed, their sha256s were recomputed
# from this commit, and the copies on disk were replaced with those bytes.
# That is the manifest's rule honoured, not skipped: advancing core_commit
# means re-checking every file already listed, not only the ones expected to
# move.
core_repo=agenticapps-eu/agenticapps-workflow-core
core_commit=ef030d0430e6c0df6dc13ab567baab3f9e006dbe

# RESOLVED at install time — not vendored in this repo.
file=bin/openspec-change-gate.sh sha256=4ad996cb7f95ebc45c35177eaad70781c23f166fb14283dc693a8ecc31476780
file=bin/run-plan-review.sh sha256=f3dae9bacc86733cd66c36d54506e7a3ae1492a58d7e1723d9bf78be6067578e
file=bin/reviewer-cli.sh sha256=9a26ebcda9f8c7e3839778337c1b56a4a421610735c08b8b5de1bb528397b11a

# VENDORED on disk — pinned so the copies are checkable against a fixed commit.
file=bin/resolve-core-artifact.sh sha256=1274598c07c0853b91c08d9b27da85d46cc754eff57b9c456cb79f293caf11ac
file=bin/install-shared-artifact.sh sha256=c5dbdbe29e211b924dbbdc6d3d25e8dde8936fac3a4f2d46ebdef59f71ed9e8a
file=tools/change-gate-conformance.sh sha256=9ddfd5d641464920a4240c656384db722b3b7738768b09cc2a0beb2a2c3aeb21
file=tools/reviewer-cli-conformance.sh sha256=f5161c8b7025e889eec0c78c3b0d6091d51e630ee2b5585d6e7c721089855011
